{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":2,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"prior finding 2","checklist_item":"- [ ] Single-source the acli version/sha256 pins between Dockerfile.mcp and the CI ACLI_VERSION/ACLI_SHA256 repo variables (or add a parity test), so the on-box image pin cannot drift from what CI validates.","criteria":["iac"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:46: `ARG ACLI_VERSION=1.3.19-stable`","infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:47-48: `ARG ACLI_SHA256_AMD64=...` / `ARG ACLI_SHA256_ARM64=...`","CI uses repo variables instead: .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:316 `ACLI_VERSION: ${{ vars.ACLI_VERSION }}` and :317 `ACLI_SHA256: ${{ vars.ACLI_SHA256 }}`","Deploy passes no build-arg override: infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:887 `docker compose build mcp`","The new test asserts a pin exists but not parity with CI: tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:160 `assert version and version != \"latest\"`","infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:48: `ARG ACLI_SHA256_ARM64=72972e74fa9036c5b40175570234a2e79559776c06a3aa29f632a39c7d3674da`","CI only fetches amd64: .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:325 `.../acli_${ACLI_VERSION}_linux_amd64.tar.gz`","Test only checks shape/count/distinctness, not value: tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:166 `re.findall(r\"ACLI_SHA256_(?:AMD64|ARM64)=([0-9a-fA-F]{64})\", text)`"],"finding":"The pinned ACLI_VERSION and per-arch sha256 digests in Dockerfile.mcp duplicate the CI-side ACLI_VERSION/ACLI_SHA256 repo variables with no single-sourcing or parity test, so the container image's acli pin can silently drift from the version CI validates against. The deploy build (`docker compose build mcp`) passes no --build-arg, so these hardcoded defaults are exactly what ships.","id":"0","impact":0.36,"location":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:46","merged_from":["The ARM64 acli sha256 (ACLI_SHA256_ARM64) — the digest that actually ships to the arm64 deploy box — has no automated cross-verification: CI only downloads and checksum-verifies the amd64 tarball, and the new manifest test only asserts the arm64 digest is present, 64 hex chars, and distinct from amd64. Its correctness is verified solely by the build-time download-and-check on the box."],"norm_id":"n698ea151be932664","priority":0.36,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-iac","reviewers":["code-review-iac"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"sometimes","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"prior finding 4","checklist_item":"- [ ] Cross-check that Dockerfile ACLI_VERSION/ACLI_SHA256 defaults match the CI repo variables, and add a mechanism (shared file or CI assertion) to prevent drift.","criteria":["supply-chain"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["ARG ACLI_VERSION=1.3.19-stable","ARG ACLI_SHA256_AMD64=f29fa8b7f01710053c2f4e07723501ebfe448672b669d32d83e961686d383a6d","PR text: 'Provisioned exactly the way CI pins it (.github/workflows/external-integration.yml, the ACLI_VERSION/ACLI_SHA256 repo variables)' — but nothing in the diff ties the Dockerfile defaults to those variables"],"finding":"The ACLI_VERSION and ACLI_SHA256_{AMD64,ARM64} pins are hardcoded as Dockerfile ARG defaults, duplicating values the PR claims live as CI repo variables (external-integration.yml ACLI_VERSION/ACLI_SHA256). There is no automated check that the Dockerfile pins match the CI-pinned source of truth, so the two can silently drift to different acli versions/checksums.","id":"1","impact":0.36,"location":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:41-43","norm_id":"n9801e21527aaa5ea","priority":0.36,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-supply-chain","reviewers":["code-review-supply-chain"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed